; A count must hold at every solution.  Two rows are (vote yes) and a third is
; (vote $v), its value not yet known: at some solution there are three yes
; votes, so "exactly two" does not hold and the rule cannot fire.  Once a rule
; fixes $v as no, the count holds.
(step one)
(vote yes) (vote yes) (vote $v)
(token)
(rule exactly-two (count 2 (vote yes)) (absent (decided)) (make (decided)))
(rule fix (take (token)) (read (vote no)) (make (fixed)))
